<http://data.silknow.org/object/42f27b59-51a1-3440-85b7-1f8b28750c91>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Furnishing fabric of crimson silk damask with a pattern of small flowers, fruits and leaves surrounding a bold, brocaded design in gold. Large leaves and palmette shapes are connected by curving stems to form a symmetrical cartouche framing a golden coronet.\n\nThe pattern appears in half drop repeat across the broad selvedges, which are woven with green and white silk."@en , "Furnishing fabric of brocaded silk damask, Italy, 17th century"@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/32eab320-c9b4-358e-b786-862614e65793> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Furnishing fabric of brocaded silk damask, Italy, 17th century"@en , "Furnishing fabric of crimson silk damask with a pattern of small flowers, fruits and leaves surrounding a bold, brocaded design in gold. Large leaves and palmette shapes are connected by curving stems to form a symmetrical cartouche framing a golden coronet.\n\nThe pattern appears in half drop repeat across the broad selvedges, which are woven with green and white silk."@en ;
